{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "שטנה", :translit "sitnah", :gloss "strife"} {:he "שטנה על ירושלים", :translit "sitnah al yerushalayim", :gloss "strife against Jerusalem"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["שטנה"]} {:kind :other, :note "The two occurrences of שטנה link this verse to Haman's accusation against Jerusalem in Ezra 4:6."}], :frame {:text "The verse reports Isaac's well was named שטנה, \"strife,\" because the shepherds of Gerar contended with Isaac's shepherds (Genesis 26:21). In Ezra 4:6 the word שטנה is used for an accusation written against the inhabitants of Judah and Jerusalem, which the Ba'al HaTurim reads as connected to Haman. The Megillah (Esther 3:8–9) records Haman's slander against the Jews, and rabbinic tradition identifies Haman as an Agagite descended from Amalek (Megillah 13a).", :sources ["Genesis 26:21" "Ezra 4:6" "Esther 3:8" "Megillah 13a"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["שטנה"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "שטנה", :refs ["Genesis 26:21" "Ezra 4:6"], :n 2, :lens :exact}]} {:kind :other, :note "The two occurrences of שטנה link this verse to Haman's accusation against Jerusalem in Ezra 4:6.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:08:20.720854249Z", :model "glm-5.2"}